// 06 · Restraint — deliberate eating, and the tragedy of the commons.
//
// 04's Hunter eats reflexively. Here the forager can CHOOSE when to eat: the `Grazer`
// brain forages exactly like a Hunter but gates its bite on its OWN hunger — it reads
// its energy reserve (PROPRIOCEPTION, the self-state channel) and eats only while it
// is below `hunger_threshold`. Two foragers share one oasis, SAME body and economy,
// differing ONLY in that appetite gate (eating is free, so nothing else separates
// them):
//   • GREEDY  (1.0) eats whatever is in range, even when full — it strips its patch;
//   • PRUDENT (0.6) stops at two-thirds full — its time-averaged draw ≈ its metabolic
//     need, so it leaves the flora alive.
//
// The driver (tests/restraint.rs) pins two results. (A) A prudent MONOCULTURE is a
// stability lever — it persists and its flora thrives, where a greedy monoculture
// overshoots and collapses to extinction. (B) But MIXED, as shipped here, greed is
// individually superior (eats more → more nutrient → more offspring), so it OUT-COMPETES
// prudence and then boom-busts the flora it dominates: the tragedy of the commons.
// Restraint stabilises but is not individually selected (making it *evolve* needs strong
// spatial viscosity — ROADMAP §9, deferred). Slow foragers, so grazing pressure sits near
// the flora's regrowth and the contrast is legible.
//
// Watch: crimson (greedy) overtakes teal (prudent), then overshoots its own oasis.
(
    tick_hz: 64.0,
    arena_half_extent: 540.0,
    archetypes: [
        (
            name: "Greedy",
            color: (0.9, 0.32, 0.36),
            count: 16,
            radius: 8.0,
            reserve_max: 120.0,
            genotype: (
                max_speed: 50.0,
